B.Yu=new A.dt("The short version","You put documents somewhere only your group can reach them, you open them in a viewer that discourages casual copying, and every open is written to a log the whole group can see. The point is not that leaking becomes impossible \u2014 it is that it stops being anonymous.",!1)
B.Yk=new A.dt("Two halves of the app","Groups and documents need an account, because they are tied to who you are.\n\nBurn Notes, Burn Files and code redemption do not. Nobody signs in on either end of those \u2014 not the sender, not the recipient.",!1)
B.Ys=new A.dt("Where things live","Workspace is your home: quick tools and your private scratchpad.\nVault is every document shared with you across all your groups.\nStudy Desk is the secure reader you open documents in.\nActivity is the audit log.\nGroups is where communities and their files live.",!1)
B.a30=s([B.Yu,B.Yk,B.Ys],t.eH)
B.a9u=s(["about","overview","start","what is this","purpose"],t.s)
B.YM=new A.ko("what-is-no-sus","What NO SUS is","A workspace for sharing study material with people you choose \u2014 and knowing what happened to it afterwards.",B.jb,B.a30,B.a9u)
B.Y7=new A.dt("Joining","You need an invite link or an invite code. Opening an invite link shows you the group name and how many members it has before you commit to anything.\n\nThere is no directory to browse. If you were not invited, you cannot find or join a group.",!1)
B.Y8=new A.dt("Creating","Groups \u2192 the + button. You become the group admin. Turning on an invite code generates a shareable 8-character code; leave it off to add people only through invite links you generate yourself.",!1)
B.Yc=new A.dt("Leaving","Open the group \u2192 the menu in the top right \u2192 Leave group. You lose access to its files immediately. Anything you uploaded stays with the group.",!1)
B.Y6=new A.dt("Global Community","Every new account joins one shared group called Global Community so the app is not empty on day one. Treat it as public: assume anyone with a NO SUS account can read what you put there. You can leave it like any other group.",!0)
B.aap=s([B.Y7,B.Y8,B.Yc,B.Y6],t.eH)
B.a7h=s(["community","join","invite","create group","leave"],t.s)
B.YQ=new A.ko("groups","Groups and communities","A group is a private space with its own members, files and activity log. You join by invite.",B.hO,B.aap,B.a7h)
B.Yy=new A.dt("Members can","Read every file in the group, upload their own, rename and delete what they uploaded, and see the full activity log.",!1)
B.Yl=new A.dt("Admins can also","Promote and demote other members, remove members, ban and unban people, delete anyone's file, manage invite links, and delete the group.",!1)
B.Yz=new A.dt("How it is enforced","By the database, not by the app. Hiding a button is a convenience; the permission check runs server-side on every write. An edited client gets a rejection, not a shortcut.",!1)
B.Yp=new A.dt("Banning","A ban removes someone and blocks them from rejoining with any invite. Unbanning lets them accept an invite again \u2014 it does not re-add them automatically.",!1)
B.a7l=s([B.Yy,B.Yl,B.Yz,B.Yp],t.eH)
B.a6p=s(["admin","member","permission","promote","demote","remove","ban","moderation"],t.s)
B.YO=new A.ko("roles","Roles and permissions","Groups have admins and members. Admins manage people and content; members read and contribute.",B.lM,B.a7l,B.a6p)
B.Y4=new A.dt("Uploading","Open a group \u2192 Files \u2192 the upload button. Everyone in that group can read it. There is no per-file audience inside a group \u2014 the group is the audience.",!1)
B.Yq=new A.dt("Reading","Tap Reveal on any file to open it in the Study Desk. Documents are streamed into memory for the session rather than saved to your device's file system.",!1)
B.Yg=new A.dt("Touch to reveal","Content sits behind a blur until you hold your finger on it. It is aimed at the person standing behind you, not at a determined attacker. Turn it off in Settings \u2192 Privacy & Security.",!1)
B.Y9=new A.dt("What this does not do","It does not encrypt files end-to-end \u2014 group documents are stored server-side and access is enforced by database rules. If that is your threat model, use Burn Files instead: those are encrypted on your device and the key never reaches the server.",!0)
B.a63=s([B.Y4,B.Yq,B.Yg,B.Y9],t.eH)
B.aag=s(["file","upload","pdf","vault","study desk","spyglass","viewer"],t.s)
B.YG=new A.ko("secure-documents","Secure documents","Files shared into a group open in a reader built to make copying awkward and attributable.",B.lI,B.a63,B.aag)
B.yt=new A.aT(61170,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Y2=new A.dt("Watermarking","Your email and a timestamp are drawn over every page you open. A photograph of the screen carries them too, which is the point: a leaked page identifies the session it came from.",!1)
B.YB=new A.dt("Screenshot blocking is Android-only","On Android the app sets the system flag that blocks screenshots and screen recording, and logs the attempt. On the web app and on iOS there is no such flag \u2014 nothing stops a screenshot there, and the app does not pretend otherwise. The watermark and the audit log are what protect you on those platforms.",!0)
B.Y3=new A.dt("A camera always wins","No app can stop someone photographing their own screen with another device. Every control here is designed for attribution after the fact, not prevention.",!0)
B.a8r=s([B.Y2,B.YB,B.Y3],t.eH)
B.a9l=s(["watermark","screenshot","screen record","capture","leak"],t.s)
B.YP=new A.ko("watermarking","Watermarks and screenshots","Open documents carry your identity on-screen, and on Android the system screenshot is blocked.",B.yt,B.a8r,B.a9l)
B.Yh=new A.dt("How it works","Your note is encrypted on your device. Only the encrypted blob is uploaded \u2014 the key is put in the link, after the # symbol, which browsers never send to a server. The first person to open the link gets the note and the stored copy is deleted.",!1)
B.YD=new A.dt("Sending the link safely","The link is the secret. Anyone who sees it can read the note, once. Send it over a different channel than the thing it protects.",!1)
B.Yv=new A.dt("It really is one read",'If a link preview service or an over-eager chat client fetches the link, it burns. The recipient then sees "already read" \u2014 which is your signal that something opened it first.',!0)
B.a7j=s([B.Yh,B.YD,B.Yv],t.eH)
B.a4O=s(["secret","self destruct","one time","password","anonymous"],t.s)
B.YN=new A.ko("burn-notes","Burn Notes","Send a secret that is destroyed the moment it is read. No account needed, on either end.",B.lK,B.a7j,B.a4O)
B.Y1=new A.dt("How it works","Each file is encrypted on your device with its own key before anything is uploaded. The keys ride in the link fragment and never reach the server. First download wins; the stored copy is then deleted.",!1)
B.Y5=new A.dt("Limits","Up to 10 files and 25 MB combined per share. Larger uploads are rejected before anything leaves your device, so a too-big file fails instantly rather than after a long upload.",!1)
B.YA=new A.dt("Short codes","A single-file share can also generate a short code for someone to type in, for when a long link is awkward. Multi-file shares are link-only.",!1)
B.a1s=s([B.Y1,B.Y5,B.YA],t.eH)
B.a9x=s(["file","anonymous","upload","self destruct","send file","size limit"],t.s)
B.YR=new A.ko("burn-files","Burn Files","The same idea as a Burn Note, for files. Encrypted on your device, deleted after one download.",B.jd,B.a1s,B.a9x)
B.YC=new A.dt("Sharing outward","A share link lets one person read one document without joining the group. They open it in a watermarked viewer \u2014 they never get the file itself.",!1)
B.Yj=new A.dt("Seeing what happened","You get a view log for each link: when it was opened and from where. If a link is opened by someone you did not send it to, that shows up.",!1)
B.Yd=new A.dt("Redeeming a code","Workspace \u2192 Redeem a Code. Codes are single-use and expire; once redeemed the content is gone for everyone, including you.",!1)
B.a7N=s([B.YC,B.Yj,B.Yd],t.eH)
B.a5w=s(["securesend","external","link","redeem","code","analytics","revoke"],t.s)
B.YJ=new A.ko("share-links","Share links and codes","Send one group document to someone outside the group, and see when they opened it.",B.qA,B.a7N,B.a5w)
B.Y0=new A.dt("What is recorded","Joins and leaves, uploads, renames, deletions, document opens, screenshot attempts, and moderation actions. Entries record who and when \u2014 never the contents of a document.",!1)
B.Ye=new A.dt("Why it is visible to everyone","Accountability only works if it is mutual. Members can see admins' actions as readily as admins see members'. Nobody gets a private log.",!1)
B.Yf=new A.dt("Tamper evidence","Entries are chained together, so removing or editing one breaks the chain and is detectable. The log is append-only \u2014 actions cannot be quietly retracted, including by admins.",!1)
B.a6S=s([B.Y0,B.Ye,B.Yf],t.eH)
B.a2W=s(["audit","log","activity","history","who opened","tamper"],t.s)
B.YI=new A.ko("audit-log","Activity and the audit log","Every meaningful action in a group is recorded, in order, visible to the whole group.",B.qz,B.a6S,B.a2W)
B.Yx=new A.dt("What you can be notified about","Invitations and join requests, role changes, moderation actions affecting you, documents shared into your groups, and security events on your account. Each category can be turned off on its own in Settings \u2192 Notifications.",!1)
B.Y_=new A.dt("Nothing sensitive on the lock screen","Notification text names the group and the kind of event \u2014 never a document's name or contents. Anyone glancing at your phone learns that something happened, not what.",!1)
B.Ym=new A.dt("If you said no to the permission","Android only asks once. Everything still appears in the in-app inbox, and Settings \u2192 Notifications has a shortcut to the system settings page if you change your mind.",!1)
B.ab0=s([B.Yx,B.Y_,B.Ym],t.eH)
B.a2h=s(["push","alert","permission","mute","lock screen","privacy"],t.s)
B.YK=new A.ko("notifications","Notifications","Get told when something you care about happens, without the details showing on your lock screen.",B.yD,B.ab0,B.a2h)
B.Yt=new A.dt("What is stored","Your email, display name and avatar choice. Documents you upload to groups. Audit entries for actions you took. That is the account; there is no advertising profile behind it.",!1)
B.Ya=new A.dt("Who can see your email","Other members of groups you are in \u2014 the audit log names people by email, which is what makes it useful. If that matters to you, be deliberate about which groups you join.",!0)
B.Yi=new A.dt("Deleting your account","Settings \u2192 Danger Zone \u2192 Delete account. It removes your profile and every group membership permanently and cannot be undone. Audit entries recording actions you took stay, because the log is append-only and other members rely on it.",!1)
B.ab3=s([B.Yt,B.Ya,B.Yi],t.eH)
B.a3u=s(["profile","password","delete account","privacy","email","data"],t.s)
B.YH=new A.ko("account","Your account and your data","What is stored about you, who can see it, and how to change or delete it.",B.yo,B.ab3,B.a3u)
B.Zt=new A.aT(61190,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Yn=new A.dt('"This link has already been opened"',"A Burn Note or Burn File is genuinely gone \u2014 that is the feature working. Ask the sender for a new one. If you never opened it, assume something else did and treat the contents as exposed.",!1)
B.Yo=new A.dt('"This invite has expired or been revoked"',"Invite links can have an expiry date and a usage limit, and an admin can revoke one. Ask for a fresh link.",!1)
B.Yr=new A.dt("A document will not open","Usually access was removed \u2014 you left the group, were removed from it, or the file was deleted. Pull to refresh; if the file is gone from the list, it was deleted.",!1)
B.Yw=new A.dt("The app says it is offline","Groups, documents and the audit log need a connection. Burn Notes and Burn Files need one too, to upload. Your private scratchpad keeps working, and syncs when you are back.",!1)
B.Yb=new A.dt("Signed out unexpectedly","If unusual security signals are detected on your account, the app asks you to sign in again. That is a refresh, not a lockout \u2014 signing back in clears the flag if the risk has passed.",!1)
B.a81=s([B.Yn,B.Yo,B.Yr,B.Yw,B.Yb],t.eH)
B.a4S=s(["error","expired","broken","cannot open","offline","stuck","failed"],t.s)
B.YL=new A.ko("troubleshooting","When something goes wrong","The failures people actually hit, and what each one means.",B.Zt,B.a81,B.a4S)
B.zI=s([B.YM,B.YQ,B.YO,B.YG,B.YP,B.YN,B.YR,B.YJ,B.YI,B.YK,B.YH,B.YL],A.af("B<ko>"))
